-## Choosing float or Float16
-
-Keep `float` (the default) when RAM is sufficient, you need more numerical precision or a wider range, or CPU time and flash matter more than sample storage. Existing sketches need no changes to keep using float.
-
-Use `grafici::Float16` when sample arrays take too much RAM and lower precision is acceptable. Each stored value takes **2 bytes instead of 4**, with roughly three significant decimal digits and a maximum finite magnitude of 65,504. It supports negative values and values above 1; arithmetic is not clamped to `[0,1]`. Calculations use float and round when stored as Float16. Conversion can add CPU work and flash usage, so this is a RAM-saving choice, not a promise of faster drawing.
-
